packages-title = Package tracking
packages-admin-title = Package tracking provider
packages-admin-help = Disabled by default. Administrators configure the provider here; each mailbox account must separately opt in. Use packages.allowed in Settings to restrict availability by domain or account.
packages-admin-provider = AfterShip Tracking
packages-admin-provider-help = Uses the fixed HTTPS AfterShip Tracking 2026-07 API. Requests follow the package-tracking outbound route and never follow redirects. Only tracking numbers and carrier codes leave Mailwoman. Provider access and billing are managed in your AfterShip account.
packages-admin-enabled = Allow opted-in accounts to contact this provider
packages-admin-key = Provider API key
packages-admin-key-help = Enter a key with tracking read and create permissions. It is sealed on the server and never returned to the browser.
packages-admin-key-retain = A key is stored. Leave empty to retain it, or enter a replacement. The existing key is never shown.
packages-admin-interval = Minimum refresh interval in seconds
packages-admin-interval-help = Between 60 and 86400 seconds for each saved package, including failed requests. Requests are manual; this does not enable background polling.
packages-admin-save = Save provider configuration
packages-admin-saved = Provider configuration saved. Accounts still need their own opt-in before sending a tracking request.
packages-privacy = Off by default. Enabling this feature lets you save packages here. Only pressing Track or refresh sends the tracking number and carrier to the administrator’s AfterShip provider. Message contents, account email addresses and package labels are never sent. Mailwoman does not scan your mailbox or poll in the background.
packages-enable = Enable package tracking for my account
packages-unavailable = Package tracking is disabled or has not been configured by your administrator.
packages-add = Add package
packages-edit = Package details
packages-label = Label
packages-trackingNumber = Tracking number
packages-carrier = Carrier code
packages-label-help = Optional private label, such as a shop or order name. This stays in Mailwoman.
packages-trackingNumber-help = Enter the carrier’s tracking number using letters, digits or hyphens.
packages-carrier-help = Use the exact AfterShip carrier code, such as ups, fedex or usps. Some carriers require additional information and cannot be tracked by this integration.
packages-save = Save package
packages-back = Back to packages
packages-save-local = Saving only stores this package in your account. Use its Track or refresh action to contact the provider.
packages-discard = Discard the unsaved package changes?
packages-history = Latest tracking events
packages-time = Carrier time
packages-location = Location
packages-event = Event
packages-status = Status
packages-estimate = Estimated delivery
packages-actions = Actions
packages-loading = Loading packages…
packages-reload = Reload saved packages
packages-edit-name = Edit { $name }
packages-refresh-name = Track or refresh { $name }
packages-remove-name = Remove { $name }
packages-remove-confirm = Remove { $name } from Mailwoman? This does not erase records already held by the tracking provider.
packages-refresh-help = Updates are requested explicitly, at most once per package every { $seconds } seconds. Provider estimates are not delivery guarantees. Carrier event times are displayed as supplied.
packages-refreshed = The package status and recent events were updated from the tracking provider.
packages-removed = The package was removed from your Mailwoman account. Existing provider records are unchanged.
packages-saved = The package was saved in your account. No tracking request was sent.
packages-preferences-saved = Your package tracking preference was saved.
packages-error-packageUnavailable = Package tracking could not be loaded. Please try again.
packages-error-packageChanged = The account or package changed. Reload before trying again.
packages-error-packageDisabled = Package tracking is disabled by your account or administrator.
packages-error-invalidPackage = Check the tracking number, carrier code and label.
packages-error-packageLimit = Your account can save up to 100 packages.
packages-error-packageDuplicate = This tracking number and carrier are already saved.
packages-error-packageNotFound = This package is no longer available. Return to the package list.
packages-error-packageBusy = Another tracking update is in progress. Please try again shortly.
packages-error-packageCooldown = This package was checked recently. Wait for the configured refresh interval.
packages-error-packageProviderUnavailable = The tracking provider could not complete the request. Check the carrier and number, then wait before retrying. Your administrator can check the provider configuration.
packages-error-packageProviderResponse = The provider returned an unexpected response. The saved package status was not replaced.
packages-status-Pending = Not yet tracked
packages-status-InfoReceived = Shipment information received
packages-status-InTransit = In transit
packages-status-OutForDelivery = Out for delivery
packages-status-AttemptFail = Delivery attempt failed
packages-status-Delivered = Delivered
packages-status-AvailableForPickup = Ready for pickup
packages-status-Exception = Delivery exception
packages-status-Expired = Tracking expired
